{"version":2,"exportedAt":1779449382987,"trip":{"id":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Masai Mara","createdAt":1779264149846,"updatedAt":1779264149846},"locations":[{"id":"6uaDAfu8iOnIEZSvCOaeD","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Masai Mara","order":3,"tags":[],"createdAt":1779264149846,"caption":"The greatest wildlife show on earth","review":"Five days was not enough. Wildebeest crossing the Mara river, lion kills at dawn, leopard in acacia tree \u2014 this is Africa.","dateFrom":1778630400000,"dateTo":1779062400000},{"id":"GSbQxFzrLMG3I3K82bSqV","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Amboseli","order":0,"tags":[],"createdAt":1779264149846,"caption":"Elephants against Kilimanjaro","review":"Absolutely stunning. Elephants against Kilimanjaro backdrop \u2014 can't beat it anywhere on earth. The dust, the heat, the pure wildness of it.","dateFrom":1778112000000,"dateTo":1778284800000},{"id":"iLGtTQHP5O2L73fCoQtL0","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Nakuru","order":2,"tags":[],"createdAt":1779264149846,"caption":"Pink flamingo paradise","review":"Flamingos beyond anything I imagined. White rhinos within 10 metres. Baboon Cliff at golden hour was jaw-dropping.","dateFrom":1778457600000,"dateTo":1778630400000},{"id":"n6SPfaMUWjhntWo5sb1FQ","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Naivasha","order":1,"tags":[],"createdAt":1779264149846,"caption":"Rift Valley lakes and Hell's Gate","review":"Cycling through Hell's Gate with zebras and buffaloes was surreal. Lake Naivasha boat trip at sunset was genuinely magical.","dateFrom":1778284800000,"dateTo":1778457600000},{"id":"sGr7KpNvX2mY4wQjTe9La","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Samburu","order":4,"tags":[],"createdAt":1779062400000,"caption":"Rugged northern Kenya wilderness","review":"Raw and dramatic \u2014 endemic species found nowhere else. Reticulated giraffe, Grevy's zebra, Beisa oryx and gerenuk all in one afternoon.","dateFrom":1779062400000,"dateTo":1779235200000},{"id":"Rb6nWcUqH3xZ5kAsDf8Vb","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Ol Pejeta","order":5,"tags":[],"createdAt":1779235200000,"caption":"Africa's largest black rhino sanctuary","review":"Seeing the last two northern white rhinos was deeply moving. Conservation at its most urgent and inspiring.","dateFrom":1779235200000,"dateTo":1779321600000},{"id":"Pq4hFtGiB7yC1rLmNj2Kc","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Nairobi","order":6,"tags":[],"createdAt":1779321600000,"caption":"The safari capital","review":"Game park inside a city is surreal \u2014 photographed lions with skyscrapers in the background. Giraffe Centre was pure joy.","dateFrom":1779321600000,"dateTo":1779408000000},{"id":"Tz8oEuMlD5vX9nQwAp3Sd","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Diani Beach","order":7,"tags":[],"createdAt":1779408000000,"caption":"Perfect white sands to end the journey","review":"After three weeks of dust and game drives, wading into warm Indian Ocean felt like a religious experience. Colobus monkeys in the trees above.","dateFrom":1779408000000,"dateTo":1779667200000}],"spots":[{"id":"I5pf144xptYsksm-S0G-K","locationId":"GSbQxFzrLMG3I3K82bSqV","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Amboseli National Park","caption":"Amazing place for wildlife photography! bring your best lens.","googlePlaceUrl":"https://share.google/65swRgXVIPiwKf2T6","order":0,"createdAt":1779266124715,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778112000000,"dateTo":1778112000000},{"id":"S-ikRds3kHL_gCdqsD_kw","locationId":"GSbQxFzrLMG3I3K82bSqV","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Mount Kilimanjaro","caption":"Best place for landscape photography.","googlePlaceUrl":"Mount Kilimanjaro","order":1,"createdAt":1779305455488,"dateFrom":1778198400000,"dateTo":1778198400000},{"id":"cSjDQYDFbBx2JWBl20yg","locationId":"GSbQxFzrLMG3I3K82bSqV","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Ol Tukai Lodge","caption":"The best positioned lodge in all of Amboseli. Elephant herds walk past the pool at dusk. Booked the banda nearest the swamp \u2014 worth every cent.","googlePlaceUrl":"Ol Tukai Lodge","order":2,"createdAt":1779269893837,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778112000000,"dateTo":1778112000000},{"id":"AI3lobhakG_SyzSue1Nh","locationId":"GSbQxFzrLMG3I3K82bSqV","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Enkongo Narok Swamp","caption":"Main water source for the whole park. Hundreds of elephants at dawn \u2014 mothers, calves, massive bulls \u2014 all silhouetted against Kilimanjaro. Photographer's paradise.","googlePlaceUrl":"Enkongo Narok Swamp","order":3,"createdAt":1779269981491,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778112000000,"dateTo":1778112000000},{"id":"rFfveashtVcNiYVn2TeA","locationId":"GSbQxFzrLMG3I3K82bSqV","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Observation Hill","caption":"360\u00b0 panoramic view: Kilimanjaro one side, swamp on the other, elephants specks below. Arrived at 5:30pm for the sunset. Didn't want to leave.","googlePlaceUrl":"Observation Hill","order":4,"createdAt":1779270069145,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778198400000,"dateTo":1778198400000},{"id":"4zL3oHL8ceu01i6H97f-","locationId":"GSbQxFzrLMG3I3K82bSqV","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Masai Cultural Village","caption":"Visited a real Masai manyatta. Bought a beautiful beaded bracelet from the women. Warriors demonstrated the adumu (jumping dance). Children were fascinated by the camera.","googlePlaceUrl":"Masai Cultural Village","order":5,"createdAt":1779270156799,"rating":4,"dateFrom":1778198400000,"dateTo":1778198400000},{"id":"wBDvGzcAbgq9EI65KoHw","locationId":"n6SPfaMUWjhntWo5sb1FQ","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Lake Naivasha Boat Trip","caption":"Early morning on the water surrounded by hippos and hundreds of bird species. African fish eagle called right overhead. Best sunrise of the trip.","googlePlaceUrl":"Lake Naivasha Boat Trip","order":0,"createdAt":1779270244453,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778284800000,"dateTo":1778284800000},{"id":"JiTt8mWk93gPnG2jneeF","locationId":"n6SPfaMUWjhntWo5sb1FQ","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Hell's Gate National Park","caption":"Cycled 4 hours through gorges where buffalo and zebra grazed alongside us. No fences, no barriers. Just you, the bike, and the wildlife.","googlePlaceUrl":"Hell's Gate National Park","order":1,"createdAt":1779270332107,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778284800000,"dateTo":1778284800000},{"id":"eAhWGdcVjUOG2MKzpiBy","locationId":"n6SPfaMUWjhntWo5sb1FQ","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Crescent Island Game Sanctuary","caption":"Walked unguided among giraffes, zebras, and wildebeest on this tiny island in the lake. Eerie and beautiful. Hippos surfacing 20 metres away.","googlePlaceUrl":"Crescent Island Game Sanctuary","order":2,"createdAt":1779270419761,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778371200000,"dateTo":1778371200000},{"id":"FrOpE-fuRfj0-um-vMMO","locationId":"n6SPfaMUWjhntWo5sb1FQ","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Elsamere Conservation Centre","caption":"Home of Joy Adamson of Born Free fame. Beautiful lakeside property. Afternoon tea served on the terrace with colobus monkeys performing overhead.","googlePlaceUrl":"Elsamere Conservation Centre","order":3,"createdAt":1779270507415,"rating":4,"dateFrom":1778371200000,"dateTo":1778371200000},{"id":"pGk0oJ7z9UJOLx_z-2bq","locationId":"n6SPfaMUWjhntWo5sb1FQ","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Fisherman's Camp","caption":"Basic campsite on the lake shore. Had the best nyama choma of the whole trip here around a bonfire with a group of overland travellers.","googlePlaceUrl":"Fisherman's Camp","order":4,"createdAt":1779270595069,"rating":4,"dateFrom":1778457600000,"dateTo":1778457600000},{"id":"-dUE8A6k_AlwOcyaekor","locationId":"n6SPfaMUWjhntWo5sb1FQ","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Geothermal Spa at Olkaria","caption":"Natural hot springs from the nearby geothermal plant. Soaked tired muscles for two hours. Strange and wonderful to feel genuine geothermal heat.","googlePlaceUrl":"Geothermal Spa at Olkaria","order":5,"createdAt":1779270682723,"rating":4,"dateFrom":1778457600000,"dateTo":1778457600000},{"id":"N4DT7HUU2ck_VqVkxCoi","locationId":"iLGtTQHP5O2L73fCoQtL0","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Lake Nakuru National Park","caption":"Over a million flamingos turn the lake bright pink from the air. White rhinos and black rhinos share the same park \u2014 rare anywhere in Africa.","googlePlaceUrl":"Lake Nakuru National Park","order":0,"createdAt":1779270770377,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778457600000,"dateTo":1778457600000},{"id":"6iJE9yCKy64Ud_JMIH7r","locationId":"iLGtTQHP5O2L73fCoQtL0","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Flamingo Viewpoint","caption":"Classic viewpoint above the lake. Arrived at 6am and had it entirely to ourselves. Pink carpet of birds stretching to every horizon.","googlePlaceUrl":"Flamingo Viewpoint","order":1,"createdAt":1779270858031,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778457600000,"dateTo":1778457600000},{"id":"f8jV1VtwU9QIyzUBIOOc","locationId":"iLGtTQHP5O2L73fCoQtL0","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Baboon Cliff","caption":"Steep cliff with panoramic views over the lake. Baboons scramble among the rocks. Ate lunch up here while white rhinos grazed far below.","googlePlaceUrl":"Baboon Cliff","order":2,"createdAt":1779270945685,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778544000000,"dateTo":1778544000000},{"id":"9JEHX_AoxeP_nWn7Jybj","locationId":"iLGtTQHP5O2L73fCoQtL0","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Makalia Waterfall","caption":"Hidden waterfall deep inside the park. Cool, shaded, completely deserted. Found leopard pugmarks in the mud beside the pool. Never saw the cat but felt watched.","googlePlaceUrl":"Makalia Waterfall","order":3,"createdAt":1779271033339,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778544000000,"dateTo":1778544000000},{"id":"cLbG-s-O4bVHMy-PURI0","locationId":"iLGtTQHP5O2L73fCoQtL0","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Lion Hill Game Lodge","caption":"Stunning lodge perched above the park. Views from every room. Watched flamingos through binoculars from the breakfast table while eating eggs and toast.","googlePlaceUrl":"Lion Hill Game Lodge","order":4,"createdAt":1779271120993,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778457600000,"dateTo":1778457600000},{"id":"LnP8cCws49ZA3gFEeJyx","locationId":"iLGtTQHP5O2L73fCoQtL0","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Nakuru Town Market","caption":"The real Kenya. Fresh produce, kikoi fabrics, mandazi, samosas and chai. Got completely lost and loved every minute of it.","googlePlaceUrl":"Nakuru Town Market","order":5,"createdAt":1779271208647,"rating":3,"dateFrom":1778630400000,"dateTo":1778630400000},{"id":"o78b2TRa1yZIWUvQ-56g","locationId":"6uaDAfu8iOnIEZSvCOaeD","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Oloolaimutia Gate","caption":"The main entry to the reserve. The gate itself felt ceremonial \u2014 crossing into the Mara is like entering another world. Three cheetahs within 10 minutes.","googlePlaceUrl":"Oloolaimutia Gate","order":0,"createdAt":1779271296301,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778630400000,"dateTo":1778630400000},{"id":"tKqZDv5Y3QlypYaYktOR","locationId":"6uaDAfu8iOnIEZSvCOaeD","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Mara River Crossing","caption":"Sat and waited 4 hours. Then 40,000 wildebeest crossed in 20 minutes. The most chaotic, violent, beautiful thing I've ever witnessed. Crocodiles everywhere.","googlePlaceUrl":"Mara River Crossing","order":1,"createdAt":1779271383955,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778716800000,"dateTo":1778716800000},{"id":"FJZuuSFwzvkO5SOvBjUs","locationId":"6uaDAfu8iOnIEZSvCOaeD","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Hippo Pool","caption":"Dozens of hippos grunting and yawning in a bend of the Mara River. The smell is unforgettable. Stayed until sunset \u2014 hippos turned gold in the light.","googlePlaceUrl":"Hippo Pool","order":2,"createdAt":1779271471609,"rating":4,"dateFrom":1778716800000,"dateTo":1778716800000},{"id":"7l-pD5wGk9_khEHXvLkn","locationId":"6uaDAfu8iOnIEZSvCOaeD","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Lion Pride at Fig Tree Camp","caption":"Found a pride of 12 lions resting under a large fig tree. Lionesses and cubs playing. A big male opened one eye, looked straight at us, went back to sleep.","googlePlaceUrl":"Lion Pride at Fig Tree Camp","order":3,"createdAt":1779271559263,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778803200000,"dateTo":1778803200000},{"id":"Cs6EfVemeO1No23vrR-6","locationId":"6uaDAfu8iOnIEZSvCOaeD","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Masai Village at Talek","caption":"Arranged by camp \u2014 a proper community visit, not a tourist show. Warriors jumped, women sold intricate beadwork, elders invited us to sit by the fire.","googlePlaceUrl":"Masai Village at Talek","order":4,"createdAt":1779271646917,"rating":4,"dateFrom":1778803200000,"dateTo":1778803200000},{"id":"EOz6b_TZZm0Pj3CUfRae","locationId":"6uaDAfu8iOnIEZSvCOaeD","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Hot Air Balloon Safari","caption":"3:30am wake-up. Worth every second. Floated over herds of elephant and giraffe at sunrise, completely silent. Champagne bush breakfast on landing.","googlePlaceUrl":"Hot Air Balloon Safari","order":5,"createdAt":1779271734571,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778889600000,"dateTo":1778889600000},{"id":"As2CHJvO5eJqPNchH2Z0","locationId":"6uaDAfu8iOnIEZSvCOaeD","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Leopard at Marsh Drive","caption":"Found a leopard dragging a freshly killed impala into an acacia. Watched for 45 minutes. Completely alone with the guide and the moment. Speechless.","googlePlaceUrl":"Leopard at Marsh Drive","order":6,"createdAt":1779271822225,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778889600000,"dateTo":1778889600000},{"id":"eBpCq3JV7FDiYexkUDGH","locationId":"6uaDAfu8iOnIEZSvCOaeD","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Governors Camp","caption":"The legendary camp. Hippos walk through camp at night. Woke to lions roaring across the river at 2am. Spent a long time just listening in the darkness.","googlePlaceUrl":"Governors Camp","order":7,"createdAt":1779271909879,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1778630400000,"dateTo":1778630400000},{"id":"eX-A8BN6nclcChgtz4aP","locationId":"sGr7KpNvX2mY4wQjTe9La","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Samburu National Reserve","caption":"Completely different ecosystem \u2014 arid scrubland instead of savanna. Saw all five Samburu Specials in one afternoon: reticulated giraffe, Grevy's zebra, Beisa oryx, gerenuk, Somali ostrich.","googlePlaceUrl":"Samburu National Reserve","order":0,"createdAt":1779271997533,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1779062400000,"dateTo":1779062400000},{"id":"V8V6hLBq3v-xJXYcUgvf","locationId":"sGr7KpNvX2mY4wQjTe9La","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Ewaso Nyiro River","caption":"The lifeline of Samburu. Crocodiles basking on every sandbank, elephants crossing at dusk, a pride of lions drinking at dawn. Spent an entire morning here.","googlePlaceUrl":"Ewaso Nyiro River","order":1,"createdAt":1779272085187,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1779062400000,"dateTo":1779062400000},{"id":"RgkMu6Y3A1K1uJCAzAjj","locationId":"sGr7KpNvX2mY4wQjTe9La","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Gerenuk Sighting Point","caption":"Watched a gerenuk stand on its hind legs to browse an acacia for 20 minutes. A giraffe-necked gazelle doing yoga. Nature's absurdity at its finest.","googlePlaceUrl":"Gerenuk Sighting Point","order":2,"createdAt":1779272172841,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1779148800000,"dateTo":1779148800000},{"id":"6sDi_jRMTAyzeurXCgcw","locationId":"sGr7KpNvX2mY4wQjTe9La","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Samburu Intrepids Camp","caption":"Excellent tented camp right on the river bank. Woke to elephants at the water's edge from my tent. Staff cooked dinner under the stars, completely off-grid.","googlePlaceUrl":"Samburu Intrepids Camp","order":3,"createdAt":1779272260495,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1779062400000,"dateTo":1779062400000},{"id":"uNa-0_qmdmbSx0WwkwbP","locationId":"sGr7KpNvX2mY4wQjTe9La","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Samburu Village","caption":"Fascinating community. The Samburu people maintain their traditions beautifully. Bought a hand-carved wooden elephant. Long conversation with an elder through the guide.","googlePlaceUrl":"Samburu Village","order":4,"createdAt":1779272348149,"rating":4,"dateFrom":1779148800000,"dateTo":1779148800000},{"id":"eM_wIxVRM-SvyOSoZCXf","locationId":"Rb6nWcUqH3xZ5kAsDf8Vb","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Ol Pejeta Conservancy","caption":"Largest black rhino sanctuary in East Africa. Also home to the last two northern white rhinos. Seriously best-run conservancy I've visited anywhere in the world.","googlePlaceUrl":"Ol Pejeta Conservancy","order":0,"createdAt":1779272435803,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1779235200000,"dateTo":1779235200000},{"id":"rGKDLFHmhqXbwBJB27Km","locationId":"Rb6nWcUqH3xZ5kAsDf8Vb","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Northern White Rhino Enclosure","caption":"Fatu and Najin \u2014 the last two northern white rhinos on Earth. Standing 5 metres from them, knowing this is the end of a species. Heavy and humbling.","googlePlaceUrl":"Northern White Rhino Enclosure","order":1,"createdAt":1779272523457,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1779235200000,"dateTo":1779235200000},{"id":"3Ghht47wCD7CuGaGi0C9","locationId":"Rb6nWcUqH3xZ5kAsDf8Vb","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Chimpanzee Sanctuary","caption":"Rescued chimps from conflict zones across Central Africa. Watching them interact through the fence \u2014 the gestures, the politics, the humour \u2014 utterly human.","googlePlaceUrl":"Chimpanzee Sanctuary","order":2,"createdAt":1779272611111,"rating":4,"dateFrom":1779235200000,"dateTo":1779235200000},{"id":"CBcXRQER4Sw5ufqF3wQr","locationId":"Rb6nWcUqH3xZ5kAsDf8Vb","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Sweetwaters Serena Camp","caption":"Camp set around a floodlit waterhole. Set up my tripod at the hide and watched wildlife come to drink for 3 uninterrupted hours. Lion pair arrived at midnight.","googlePlaceUrl":"Sweetwaters Serena Camp","order":3,"createdAt":1779272698765,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1779235200000,"dateTo":1779235200000},{"id":"x8mtApt1Ff2oYdQLM-Vv","locationId":"Rb6nWcUqH3xZ5kAsDf8Vb","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Night Game Drive","caption":"Porcupines, spring hares, serval cat, two aardvarks. The bush after dark has an entirely different cast. Red-eyed glow of animals in the spotlight.","googlePlaceUrl":"Night Game Drive","order":4,"createdAt":1779272786419,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1779321600000,"dateTo":1779321600000},{"id":"Zup0hEJNjOG2b9l0G1lu","locationId":"Pq4hFtGiB7yC1rLmNj2Kc","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Nairobi National Park","caption":"Only city on earth with a full game reserve inside it. Photographed lions with the Nairobi CBD behind them. Rhinos against office blocks. Genuinely surreal.","googlePlaceUrl":"Nairobi National Park","order":0,"createdAt":1779272874073,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1779321600000,"dateTo":1779321600000},{"id":"0g7UqBcjPXmSyI1plB-A","locationId":"Pq4hFtGiB7yC1rLmNj2Kc","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"David Sheldrick Elephant Orphanage","caption":"Baby orphaned elephants raised by keepers who sleep beside them in the mud. Most heartwarming hour of the entire three weeks. Bought a foster certificate.","googlePlaceUrl":"David Sheldrick Elephant Orphanage","order":1,"createdAt":1779272961727,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1779321600000,"dateTo":1779321600000},{"id":"jwkpSjwm-FtA0x0yq5c6","locationId":"Pq4hFtGiB7yC1rLmNj2Kc","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Giraffe Centre","caption":"Fed a Rothschild giraffe from my hand. Enormous tongue, the gentlest eyes. Got a giraffe kiss on the forehead. Pure joy.","googlePlaceUrl":"Giraffe Centre","order":2,"createdAt":1779273049381,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1779408000000,"dateTo":1779408000000},{"id":"rIT9xIxJ1_78dp8KjN7o","locationId":"Pq4hFtGiB7yC1rLmNj2Kc","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Carnivore Restaurant","caption":"Legendary institution. Meats arrive on Maasai swords directly to the table \u2014 crocodile, ostrich, game sausage, nyama choma. Left comically full.","googlePlaceUrl":"Carnivore Restaurant","order":3,"createdAt":1779273137035,"rating":4,"dateFrom":1779408000000,"dateTo":1779408000000},{"id":"GDJy1kCWM5swtieGtL9_","locationId":"Pq4hFtGiB7yC1rLmNj2Kc","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Nairobi National Museum","caption":"Outstanding collection on Kenyan natural history. The 'Kenya: Origins' exhibit is beautifully curated. The fossilised KNM-ER 1470 skull alone is worth the visit.","googlePlaceUrl":"Nairobi National Museum","order":4,"createdAt":1779273224689,"rating":4,"dateFrom":1779321600000,"dateTo":1779321600000},{"id":"jFG-ZYRk6BLgt1hfuwFF","locationId":"Pq4hFtGiB7yC1rLmNj2Kc","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Java House Westlands","caption":"Best coffee in Nairobi. Sat for two hours journaling the whole trip. Proper espresso after weeks of safari camp instant. Small mercy.","googlePlaceUrl":"Java House Westlands","order":5,"createdAt":1779273312343,"rating":4,"dateFrom":1779408000000,"dateTo":1779408000000},{"id":"F2fydPmt0djtZEO5oCkY","locationId":"Tz8oEuMlD5vX9nQwAp3Sd","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Diani Beach","caption":"40km of white sand with almost no crowds. After three weeks of dust, wading into warm Indian Ocean felt like a religious experience. The water is that colour.","googlePlaceUrl":"Diani Beach","order":0,"createdAt":1779273399997,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1779408000000,"dateTo":1779408000000},{"id":"U6ca_umFJVMIWqD5UMi8","locationId":"Tz8oEuMlD5vX9nQwAp3Sd","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Colobus Conservation Centre","caption":"Black-and-white colobus monkeys in the forest canopy above the beach road. The team explains the threats from coastal development. Surprisingly moving little place.","googlePlaceUrl":"Colobus Conservation Centre","order":1,"createdAt":1779273487651,"rating":4,"dateFrom":1779494400000,"dateTo":1779494400000},{"id":"mNg5mDX6LRI2oRMDBaJB","locationId":"Tz8oEuMlD5vX9nQwAp3Sd","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Kisite-Mpunguti Marine Park","caption":"Boat trip out to snorkel coral reefs. Spinner dolphins followed the boat for 30 minutes. Sea turtles, napoleon wrasse, white-tipped reef shark. Mask fogged from smiling.","googlePlaceUrl":"Kisite-Mpunguti Marine Park","order":2,"createdAt":1779273575305,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1779494400000,"dateTo":1779494400000},{"id":"Yb1uaeGO00g3g0DLWnd4","locationId":"Tz8oEuMlD5vX9nQwAp3Sd","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Ali Barbour's Cave Restaurant","caption":"Dinner inside an actual ancient coral cave. Lit entirely by candles. Fresh seafood, sound of the ocean right outside. Most romantic meal of my life, eaten alone.","googlePlaceUrl":"Ali Barbour's Cave Restaurant","order":3,"createdAt":1779273662959,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1779580800000,"dateTo":1779580800000},{"id":"jm1IrvIuThxrW1G5eRql","locationId":"Tz8oEuMlD5vX9nQwAp3Sd","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Diani Reef Beach Resort","caption":"The trip's final splurge. Infinity pool spilling toward the ocean, four-poster beds with fans, fresh-caught fish served on the beach. Earned every bit of it.","googlePlaceUrl":"Diani Reef Beach Resort","order":4,"createdAt":1779273750613,"rating":5,"dateFrom":1779408000000,"dateTo":1779408000000},{"id":"zm5OHS2Ri_hilAQikD3d","locationId":"Tz8oEuMlD5vX9nQwAp3Sd","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","name":"Forty Thieves Beach Bar","caption":"The classic Diani institution. Ice-cold Tusker, sand between toes, warm evening breeze. Watched local fishermen haul in their catch as the sun went down.","googlePlaceUrl":"Forty Thieves Beach Bar","order":5,"createdAt":1779273838267,"rating":4,"dateFrom":1779667200000,"dateTo":1779667200000}],"memories":[{"id":"E5imInSKnyWXeJhVoAdFp","locationId":"GSbQxFzrLMG3I3K82bSqV","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","spotId":"I5pf144xptYsksm-S0G-K","type":"photo","blobKey":"blob-E5imInSKnyWXeJhVoAdFp","thumbnailKey":"thumb-E5imInSKnyWXeJhVoAdFp","mimeType":"image/jpeg","fileName":"images.jpg","fileSize":6587,"createdAt":1779266187593,"caption":"White Elephant"},{"id":"IeXFTDTVeKQtAOBns5dNS","locationId":"GSbQxFzrLMG3I3K82bSqV","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","type":"photo","blobKey":"blob-IeXFTDTVeKQtAOBns5dNS","thumbnailKey":"thumb-IeXFTDTVeKQtAOBns5dNS","mimeType":"image/webp","fileName":"Alone-Maasai-Warrior-at-Amboseli-National-Park-1024x683-1.webp","fileSize":54020,"createdAt":1779266246798},{"id":"Who4YvVMUliLUpokdvzUP","locationId":"GSbQxFzrLMG3I3K82bSqV","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","spotId":"I5pf144xptYsksm-S0G-K","type":"photo","blobKey":"blob-Who4YvVMUliLUpokdvzUP","thumbnailKey":"thumb-Who4YvVMUliLUpokdvzUP","mimeType":"image/webp","fileName":"Alone-Maasai-Warrior-at-Amboseli-National-Park-1024x683-1.webp","fileSize":54020,"createdAt":1779266187593,"caption":"Amboseli guy"}],"routes":[{"id":"7d01iiALsIEntDhH6ZQT6","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","fromLocationId":"n6SPfaMUWjhntWo5sb1FQ","toLocationId":"iLGtTQHP5O2L73fCoQtL0","order":1},{"id":"WGGZVYGsGkRkumV_HTyQS","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","fromLocationId":"GSbQxFzrLMG3I3K82bSqV","toLocationId":"n6SPfaMUWjhntWo5sb1FQ","order":0},{"id":"WoAZ-IEsIo6-B7oXUKFIC","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","fromLocationId":"iLGtTQHP5O2L73fCoQtL0","toLocationId":"6uaDAfu8iOnIEZSvCOaeD","order":2},{"id":"Lm97DQnosSn-emfXxEuO","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","fromLocationId":"6uaDAfu8iOnIEZSvCOaeD","toLocationId":"sGr7KpNvX2mY4wQjTe9La","order":3},{"id":"jNkTMyNKcHNH4VyoiZSM","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","fromLocationId":"sGr7KpNvX2mY4wQjTe9La","toLocationId":"Rb6nWcUqH3xZ5kAsDf8Vb","order":4},{"id":"-DUVneMhy43hfo0bogiH","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","fromLocationId":"Rb6nWcUqH3xZ5kAsDf8Vb","toLocationId":"Pq4hFtGiB7yC1rLmNj2Kc","order":5},{"id":"93UovTZbk5hPvP3LzuNO","tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","fromLocationId":"Pq4hFtGiB7yC1rLmNj2Kc","toLocationId":"Tz8oEuMlD5vX9nQwAp3Sd","order":6}],"canvasLayout":{"tripId":"G38haYh8_1G9ZS3RNz8Ls","nodes":[{"locationId":"GSbQxFzrLMG3I3K82bSqV","position":{"x":714.4444444444437,"y":-51.111111111111185},"width":280,"height":180,"zIndex":1},{"locationId":"n6SPfaMUWjhntWo5sb1F